{"id": "1470314770635952260", "channel_id": "1326453763355185215", "author_id": "702167871144591461", "author_name": "_venush", "content": "Isidora is a fictional city described in Italo Calvino’s 1972 novel *Invisible Cities*\nIsidora is a city filled with the physical embodiment of the perfect desires of youth.  Desires of learning, culture, beauty, sex, impromptu violence…anything that might swirl around in a young traveler’s heart and mind. \nWanda’s city is supposed to be based on this if I still remember it right", "timestamp": "2026-02-09T07:05:58.447000+00:00", "type": 19, "mentions": ["1376763322568937562"], "reply_to": "1470303579528233003"}
{"id": "1470315285440364544", "channel_id": "1326453763355185215", "author_id": "702167871144591461", "author_name": "_venush", "content": "back then when Wanda first debuted I have a discussion with some people here about Wanda references \n- The name Wanda is from the Wanda in Venus in Furs, which is referenced in her E3 name\n- The city is based on the The Isidora City from Italo Calvino’s novel\n- Her profile also has bible elements", "timestamp": "2026-02-09T07:08:01.186000+00:00"}
{"id": "1470315357234528289", "channel_id": "1326453763355185215", "author_id": "702167871144591461", "author_name": "_venush", "content": "so our conclusion back then is that the city name is Isidora", "timestamp": "2026-02-09T07:08:18.303000+00:00"}
